265	// An unterminated (waiting) message keeps its exact destination across a
266	// reopen: an identical-byte resubmit returns the existing record with its
267	// status, attempts and retry schedule, while changing one destination byte —
268	// or submitting the visually similar U+FFFD — is a content conflict that
269	// leaves the original record untouched.
