377	// Existing state directories keep their meaning: destinations an older build
378	// saved as plain JSON are read at face value. A saved U+FFFD is that
379	// character, not the 0xFF the old build may have lost — resubmitting the
380	// character is idempotent, while the original invalid bytes are a different
381	// destination that neither conflicts with nor merges into the saved record.
